     "n": 1,
     "code": "# Grasp the yellow pen across its narrow side\ncandidates = grasp_candidates(\"yellow_pen\")\n# Filter or pick a good grasp candidate across the short axis\ncand = min(candidates, key=lambda c: c[\"squeeze_width\"])\nres = grasp(cand)\n\nobs = observe()\nholder = obs[\"zones\"][\"magenta_holder\"]\nhx, hy, hz = holder[\"center\"]\nrim_h = holder.get(\"rim_height\", 0.08)\ntable_z = obs[\"table_z\"]\n\n# Carry the pen above the holder well above the rim\ncarry_to(hx, hy, height=rim_h + 0.15)\n\n# Orient gripper to tilt/insert vertically or lower down into holder\n# When grasped across its width (fingers pointing down), the pen is horizontal (along the side axis).\n# To make it stand upright inside the holder:\n# We need the pen axis vertical. The pen is along side = approach x finger_axis.\n# If approach is horizontal (e.g. [1, 0, 0] or [0, 1, 0]) and finger_axis is horizontal,\n# then side = approach x finger_axis points along Z (vertical)!\n# Let's rotate gripper so approach is horizontal and fingers close along vertical or horizontal.\n# Specifically, approach = [0, 1, 0], finger_axis = [1, 0, 0] gives side = [0, 0, -1] (vertical).\n# Check IK for orienting the pen vertically above the cup:\ntarget_z = table_z + rim_h + 0.10\napproach = [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]\nfinger_axis = [1.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n\nik = solve_ik(hx, hy, target_z, approach=approach, finger_axis=finger_axis)\nif not ik[\"reachable\"]:\n    approach = [1.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n    finger_axis = [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]\n\n# Move gripper to position pen vertically above holder opening\nmove_gripper(hx, hy, target_z, approach=approach, finger_axis=finger_axis, path=\"line\")\n\n# Lower down into the holder\nlower_until_contact()\n\n# Release and retreat\nopen_gripper()\nretreat(dz=0.15)\ngo_home()\ncheck(\"yellow_pen\", \"magenta_holder\")",
